# Vercel only needs to serve the static frontend (index.html + generated
# env.js). Everything below is the Python backend (deployed separately on
# Render) — without this file, Vercel's zero-config detection sees the
# top-level `api/` folder full of .py files plus requirements.txt at the
# root and auto-wraps api/main.py as a Python Serverless Function, bundling
# the *entire* requirements.txt (numpy/pandas/scikit-learn/spaCy/Airflow/
# Playwright...) into it — that's what blew past the 500MB function limit.
api/
models/
pipeline/
research/
docs/
scripts/
requirements.txt
requirements-api.txt
schema.sql
schema_migration_002.sql
schema_migration_003.sql
seed_demo.sql
.github/
.venv/
README.md
